{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Standardized financial statements for one company from its SEC EDGAR XBRL filings \u2014 revenue, net income, EPS, cash flow, and balance-sheet concepts per fiscal period, latest periods first. Use for period-by-period statements; use get_metric_history instead for one concept's long time series, and list_financial_concepts to see which concepts exist. Read-only; no API key. Values are cleaned: when a period was reported more than once the latest filing wins, fiscal periods are verified, and values computed from reported components carry derived:true plus a 'derived:' source tag \u2014 this includes Q4 figures, derived as fiscal year minus Q1\u2013Q3 because quarterly filings never contain a filed Q4 (a restated FY or quarter changes the derived value, so derived Q4 can differ from a Q4 filed later). Responses also carry a staleness flag when SEC submissions show a newer filing than the stored facts, and predecessor companies when a ticker moved between filers (e.g. a reorg), whose history is included in the periods. Every value carries per-value provenance (form, filed date, accession number). Identify the company by ticker or CIK (CIK wins if both are given). Coverage loads progressively \u2014 roughly 25 more companies refreshed per day, priority tiers first \u2014 so a valid company can legitimately return 'no financials stored yet'.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"cik":{"description":"SEC CIK number (takes precedence over ticker)","type":"number"},"limit":{"default":5,"description":"Number of periods (default 5, max 20)","type":"number"},"period":{"default":"annual","description":"Annual (10-K) periods, quarterly (10-Q) periods, or all. Default: annual","enum":["annual","quarterly","all"],"type":"string"},"ticker":{"description":"Ticker symbol, e.g. 'NVDA'","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"get_financials","outputSchema":{"properties":